From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: fix HFI Gen1 firmware crash and skip the SM8350 encoder

Fix several bugs in the Qualcomm Iris video driver for HFI Gen1
(SM8250/SM8350):
1. iris_hfi_gen1_queue_input_buffer() built the compressed and
   uncompressed empty-buffer packets on the stack without zeroing them,
   so the uncompressed packet sent uninitialized extradata_buffer and
   data IOVAs to the firmware, which crashed it (0xdeadbead).
2. Do not register the encoder video node on SM8350. The SM8350 VPU
   firmware (vpu20_4v on the Galaxy Z Flip3) crashes when /dev/video1 is
   opened, and the cause has not been found yet. SM8250 uses the same
   HFI Gen1 encoder path upstream and keeps it; so do the other
   platforms.
3. iris_set_profile_level_gen1() sent V4L2 profile and level values
   where the firmware expects HFI bitmasks, and passed sizeof(u32)
   instead of sizeof(struct hfi_profile_level). Map them (the bit values
   match the venus driver's hfi_helper.h), including H.264 Constrained
   High.
4. Send REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME only when the client asked for one, not
   unconditionally during session init, and pass the requested sync
   frame type to the firmware.
5. iris_hfi_gen1_set_frame_rate() skipped the OUTPUT queue for the
   encoder too; only the decoder should skip it.
6. Add NULL checks in iris_get_int_buf_tbl() and iris_vidc to prevent
   a kernel panic on close after a firmware failure.
7. Log the SFR diagnostic message on an HFI system error.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
